What are the three Eras of computing?
Era of tabulation, programming then AI

->The datas which are collected but never used for any purpose is called DARK DATA
->The data (information) about the other data is called META DATA

Three types of data
->Structured : These are the well organized and clean data which is less complex and easy to analyse 
Eg: Names, Data, Address

->Unstructured : These are also called dark data and doesnt have proper meaning or relation (not organized) 
Eg: Images, Videos, messages

->Semi-structured : These lies between structured and unstructed in which they are more complex then structured and yet easier to store 
than unstructured, these uses meta data to identify the real data
Eg: videos from youtube are unstructured but they are made semi by having a caption/hashtag to identify the video

->Almost 80% of the datas are dark data and 95% of the companies are working on it to make it structured and stuff

Why machine learning is better than programmable computers?
ML can predict and learn.

->Programmable computers are deterministic either they say YES or NO and actions are taken accordingly (binary)
But ML is probabilistic - its a wave between 0 to 1, it says response like "I'm 86% sure that this could happen"

How does ML learn, their types
->Supervised learning
Eg: An image (data) is provided and then its labelled as dog - several times, after training it know what dog exactly is

->Unsupervised learning 
Datas are given without any labelling and ML itself somehow finds the relation between datas and makes a clusters (several group)
which aren't exact correct answer
- This type is used when the human itself does'nt know the relation or label of the data

->Reinforcement learning
Trial and Error approach - Eg: mouse maze solver - hit wall = point-10, propogation towards goal = points+10



